@SYSTEM_TITLE
; Plain `=` on a string variable is a FORM string literal: a comma in the
; RHS is a literal character of the assigned string, never a value-list
; separator. Pre-fix `master` got this wrong — the plain-`=`-on-string
; branch parsed its RHS with the comma-*stopping* `form_arg_expr` (meant
; for call-argument lists), so it silently truncated at the first
; unescaped comma (`STR = Strawberry, Melon, Blue Hawaii` would have
; stored only `Strawberry`). This fixture pins the fix: the same branch
; now uses `form_assign_expr` (no comma stop), so the comma survives as a
; literal character. eraTHYMKR relies on this exact distinction 87 times
; (RESULTS/LOCALS/CSTR/TSTR/STR/COM_NAME) and never uses `'=` on those
; variables for a bulk fill — see `bulk_array_assign.erb`'s `A:10 = 1, 2,
; 3` for that separate, `'=`/plain-`=`-on-int-array batch-fill feature
; (docs/research/emuera-wiki/exetc.md, "Assignment to a String Variable
; Using a String Expression": "The string `Strawberry, Melon, Blue
; Hawaii` is assigned to STR:20").
STR = Strawberry, Melon, Blue Hawaii
PRINTFORML %STR%
